| **Step** | `create-again` |
| **What was checked** | Create an EHR with the same ehr\_id again. |
| **Expected** | status 409 |
| **Received** | status 201 |
| **Exchange** | `PUT http://sut/ehr/3f2a` answered 201, recording entry 2 |
| **Whose problem** | The server. A failed row counts against the claimed capability. |
| **Inputs** | `ehr_id` = `"id-1"` |
| **Upstream report** | [#42](https://github.com/Vernum-Projecten/Veredictum/issues/42) |

**Why it is required:** [specs/openehr/ITS-REST/specifications/responses/409\_EHR\_with\_id.yaml, description](https://example.org/409_EHR_with_id.yaml)

> Can happen when the supplied \`ehr\_id\` is already used by an existing EHR.

